    "desc": "The lives of non-elite individuals and groups living under the Roman Empire, seen through material evidence and its interpretation. Identity, urbanism, economy, agriculture, diet, religion, Romanization, and burial. CNRS 104, AMNE 170 or ARCL 203 recommended as preparation. Credit will be granted for only one of CNRS 206 or AMNE 278. Equivalency: CNRS 206.",
    "prer": "None"
